	This is a list of the projects Tunix is built on, used by, or learned
	from. Tunix would not boot, run a desktop, or pass its tests without them.

	Entries are sorted by name. The fields are the name (N), the web page (W),
	the license of the part Tunix uses (L), and a description (D).

----------

N: ACPICA
W: https://github.com/acpica/acpica
L: Intel ACPI license, or GPL-2.0, or BSD-3-Clause
D: iasl, which compiles the firmware model in testsuites/acpi-tests

N: kbd
W: https://kbd-project.org
L: GPL, as stated in kbd's README.eurlatgr
D: The eurlatgr console font, based on latarcyrheb-sun16, whose glyphs
D: kernel/tty/terminal_font.c draws

N: Limine
W: https://github.com/limine-bootloader/limine
L: BSD-2-Clause
D: The bootloader on every image and the boot protocol the x86_64
D: kernel enters through, kernel/arch/x86_64/limine_entry.c

N: Linux
W: https://kernel.org
L: GPL-2.0
D: The system call ABI Tunix implements so that an unmodified userland
D: runs, and the model for its virtual terminals, sysfs and procfs

N: mdBook
W: https://github.com/rust-lang/mdBook
L: MPL-2.0
D: Builds the documentation in docs/

N: QEMU
W: https://www.qemu.org
L: GPL-2.0
D: The machine every test, CI boot and development session runs on

N: uACPI
W: https://github.com/uACPI/uACPI
L: MIT
D: The AML interpreter behind the ACPI subsystem, fetched by
D: kernel/subprojects/uacpi/RECIPE and compiled into the kernel

N: Void Linux
W: https://voidlinux.org
L: Each package under its own license
D: The userland on every image: runit, xbps, Weston, GNOME, Mesa,
D: Firefox and the rest, installed unmodified by tools/sysroot.sh
